  "finalCues": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "The wise woman builds her house, but with her own hands the foolish one tears hers down.",
      "start": 2.02,
      "end": 7.717
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "Whoever fears the LORD walks uprightly, but those who despise him are devious in their ways.",
      "start": 8.64,
      "end": 14.759
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "A fool’s mouth lashes out with pride, but the lips of the wise protect them.",
      "start": 15.5,
      "end": 21.059
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "Where there are no oxen, the manger is empty, but from the strength of an ox come abundant harvests.",
      "start": 21.8,
      "end": 29.119
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "An honest witness does not deceive, but a false witness pours out lies.",
      "start": 29.98,
      "end": 34.739
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "The mocker seeks wisdom and finds none, but knowledge comes easily to the discerning.",
      "start": 35.72,
      "end": 40.639
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "Stay away from a fool, for you will not find knowledge on their lips.",
      "start": 41.44,
      "end": 45.899
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "The wisdom of the prudent is to give thought to their ways, but the folly of fools is deception.",
      "start": 46.64,
      "end": 52.439
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "Fools mock at making amends for sin, but goodwill is found among the upright.",
      "start": 53.322,
      "end": 59.479
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "Each heart knows its own bitterness, and no one else can share its joy.",
      "start": 60.22,
      "end": 65.039
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "The house of the wicked will be destroyed, but the tent of the upright will flourish.",
      "start": 65.74,
      "end": 70.059
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "There is a way that appears to be right, but in the end it leads to death.",
      "start": 70.76,
      "end": 75.54
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "Even in laughter the heart may ache, and rejoicing may end in grief.",
      "start": 76.14,
      "end": 80.579
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "The faithless will be fully repaid for their ways, and the good rewarded for theirs.",
      "start": 81.623,
      "end": 86.439
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "The simple believe anything, but the prudent give thought to their steps.",
      "start": 87.18,
      "end": 91.178
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "The wise fear the LORD and shun evil, but a fool is hotheaded and yet feels secure.",
      "start": 91.88,
      "end": 98.139
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "A quick-tempered person does foolish things, and the one who devises evil schemes is hated.",
      "start": 98.8,
      "end": 104.59
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "The simple inherit folly, but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.",
      "start": 104.98,
      "end": 109.8
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "Evildoers will bow down in the presence of the good, and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.",
      "start": 109.8,
      "end": 115.199
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "The poor are shunned even by their neighbors, but the rich have many friends.",
      "start": 115.88,
      "end": 120.299
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "It is a sin to despise one’s neighbor, but blessed is the one who is kind to the needy.",
      "start": 121.38,
      "end": 127.3
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Do not those who plot evil go astray? But those who plan what is good find love and faithfulness.",
      "start": 128.06,
      "end": 134.88
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "All hard work brings a profit, but mere talk leads only to poverty.",
      "start": 135.964,
      "end": 140.819
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "The wealth of the wise is their crown, but the folly of fools yields folly.",
      "start": 141.64,
      "end": 146.559
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "A truthful witness saves lives, but a false witness is deceitful.",
      "start": 147.48,
      "end": 151.959
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "Whoever fears the LORD has a secure fortress, and for their children it will be a refuge.",
      "start": 152.76,
      "end": 158.56
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, turning a person from the snares of death.",
      "start": 159.882,
      "end": 165.25
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "A large population is a king’s glory, but without subjects a prince is ruined.",
      "start": 165.72,
      "end": 171.48
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "Whoever is patient has great understanding, but one who is quick-tempered displays folly.",
      "start": 172.34,
      "end": 177.539
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "A heart at peace gives life to the body, but envy rots the bones.",
      "start": 178.44,
      "end": 183.219
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "Whoever oppresses the poor shows contempt for their Maker, but whoever is kind to the needy honors God.",
      "start": 183.98,
      "end": 190.979
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "When calamity comes, the wicked are brought down, but even in death the righteous seek refuge in God.",
      "start": 191.82,
      "end": 198.359
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "Wisdom reposes in the heart of the discerning and even among fools she lets herself be known.",
      "start": 199.1,
      "end": 205.159
    },
    {
      "verse": 34,
      "text": "Righteousness exalts a nation, but sin condemns any people.",
      "start": 206.18,
      "end": 211.219
    },
    {
      "verse": 35,
      "text": "A king delights in a wise servant, but a shameful servant arouses his fury.",
      "start": 212.18,
      "end": 217.519
    }
  ],
